Sec. 30001 amends Section 1017(a)(2)(A)(iii) of the Consumer Financial Protection Act of 2010 (12 U.S.C. 5497(a)(2)(A)(iii)) by striking "12" and inserting "6.5." This caps the Bureau of Consumer Financial Protection's funding at 6.5 percent (down from 12 percent) of the amount of the Bureau's funding request for the prior fiscal year, as adjusted for inflation. [end of text]


